  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 1236 AM CDT Tue Sep 8 2026\n\nNot much change expected in the long term as the strong upper level \nridge eventually breaks down over the northern part of the country. \nHowever, it will continue to control the weather across the southern \nstates. We will remain under southeasterly low level flow which will \ncontinue to keep hot, moist air over South-Central Texas. \nAdditionally, we could see some seabreeze convection occur daily \nthrough the rest of the week mainly over the Coastal Plains, but \nchances remain rather low. Otherwise expect the majority of our area \nto remain hot and dry with highs in the upper 90s to near 100 each \nday and lows in the low to mid 70s. We could likely see heat indices \njust shy of heat advisory criteria (108+ degrees) as moisture will \nremain across the area. Continue to check back to future forecasts \nand remember to practice safe heat safety.",
